will Black Adam and Shazam ever Clash on  screen it has almost happened a couple  of times but one person stood in the way  Dwayne Johnson here's why I put the  kibosh on this Clash of the Titans the  2022 release of Black Adam was a  culmination of years of production  beginning with Dwayne Johnson being cast  in the titular role all the way back in  2007. Black Adam's arrival on the big  screen was preceded by the 2019 film  Shazam that film followed the story of a  foster child named Billy Batson who gets  infused with superpowers including  flight and invulnerability by a wizard  in the comics Shazam and Black Adam are  Arch enemies who got their powers from  the same Source but opted for different  paths afterward I kneel before no one  with both characters now officially in  the DC extended Universe many comic book  fans have been eager to see the two  square off against one another but it  appears that confrontation isn't  happening anytime soon Johnson is  reportedly next to planned Black Adam  appearance in the Shazam sequel Shazam  Fury of the Gods film reporter Umberto  Gonzalez tweeted using Johnson's  nickname Rock passed on doing a cameo  and Shazam 2 when he was asked Johnson's  decision isn't necessarily a surprise he  doesn't seem to be big on the character  of Shazam despite his historical  connection to Black Adam the 2019 film  Shazam was poised to introduce Black  Adam in a scene where the newly  superpowered members of the Shazam  family sat on their Thrones before  realizing there was a seventh seed that  sat empty the rap reported that Johnson  quashed the scene as well as any other  reference to Black Adam in the film and  an August 2022 Vanity Fair interview  Johnson confirmed that Black Adam  originally had a prominent part in  Shazam he noted that the script  originally served as an origin story for  both characters but he wasn't open to  such an arrangement he explained when I  read that I just knew in my gut we can't  make this movie like this we would be  doing Black Adam and incredible  disservice it would have been fine for  Shazam having two Origin stories  converge in one movie but not good for  Black Adam Johnson said that he made a  call to Warner Brothers Executives and  insisted they separate the characters  allowing Shazam to develop its own tone  independent to Black Adam the hierarchy  of power in the DC Universe  is about to change fandom wire caught up  with Zachary Levi who plays Shazam at  Comic-Con Portugal in December 2022 and  asked him about whether Black Adam and  Shazam would meet on screen Levi  responded that he has no idea whether  the two characters would get a chance to  interact and has no influence over how  the story would play out it did  playfully point out though that if he  had the opportunity to punch Dwayne  Johnson in the face he would take it The  Hollywood Reporter called a sequel to  Black Adam unlikely now that James Gunn  and Peter Safran have taken over as the  new heads of DC Studios it's one of a  slate to planned projects that two have  reportedly scrapped while on stage at  Comic-Con Portugal Levi was asked about  his own character's cinematic future  Levi responded that gun and saffron are  friends of his and joked that friendship  would be in Jeopardy if they didn't have  Shazam as a part of their plans for DC  going forward in an interview with  collider Shazam and Shazam Fury the gods  director David F Sandberg was also asked  about plans for Black Adam and Shazam to  interact in future films he responded  that he has not been involved in any  conversations about the two characters  coming face to face adding that both  characters were on their own  trajectories at the moment  [Music]
 

